# Wave W17-W (Mt. Apex — North): zenith flags — high-gallery flags, sky-lit pale: the brightest floor in the mountain, pale cool flags whose joints are rimed with frost drawn in pale lines, winter creeping in from the east door across the stone (design: the mountain’s top floor, the north opening blazing with open sky, frost creeping in from the snowy east door — the frost lives in the floor kind’s art, art layer only). Mt. Apex — North’s own floor — split from Central’s spine flags by value entire (sky-pale vs gallery-deep) and from every shipped snow ground by kind: this is dressed stone under frost, not a snowfield.
